From 1d536de42f6d90916d4f67bc07349d7861ed1b59 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 11:35:27 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 01/18] Round 1: Add the typed score-matrix API

Add Prepared::score_matrix, which evaluates row-major untraced
parameter rows and returns typed MatrixScore values without candidate
JSON or result JSON. The Python binding releases the GIL and returns
scores (NaN unless complete), statuses and steps; the wrapper accepts
lists of lists or 2-D NumPy arrays. Inline and scoped-worker dispatch
is shared with the JSON path. The benchmark gains a CRAFT_MATRIX mode,
performance_pair.py gains --before-matrix/--after-matrix, and
optimize_performance.py gains --matrix.

Workload: serial (96 candidates, one worker), 0.2.0 lean scores_json
before, matrix after, 11 samples.
Before median: 0.225 ms. After median: 0.186 ms. Speedup: 1.21x.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
